The New Delhi Declaration was adopted, advancing cooperation on reformed multilateralism, digital public infrastructure, and clean energy. Leaders discussed expanding BRICS influence and de-dollarization roadmap for Global South trade.', 'Critical for UPSC GS-II (International Relations), State PSC Mains, and Banking GK. BRICS, Global South, and India Presidency are recurring exam topics.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529107386315-e1a2ed48a620?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'International', '["UPSC","State PSC","Banking","SSC","Railway"]', '["BRICS","India Presidency","International Relations","Global South","New Delhi Declaration"]', 'https://mea.gov.in', '2026-09-12 18:30:00.000', 1, 1, NULL, '2026-09-22 17:23:10.945', '2026-09-22 17:23:10.945'),
  ('ec9d88a1-c9c0-47c1-aafb-e40bf7915491', 'India GDP at 7.8% in Q1 FY2026-27; Rupee Falls to Rs.95/USD on Crude Oil Shock', 'India recorded 7.8% real GDP in Q1 FY2026-27. Rupee fell beyond Rs.95/USD amid Strait of Hormuz oil disruptions. RBI repo rate at 5.25%; CPI inflation rising for 3 months. Economists warn of middle-income trap.', '["Q1 FY2026-27 Real GDP Growth: 7.8% — fastest-growing major economy globally","RBI Repo Rate: 5.25%; CPI inflation rising for 3 consecutive months","Rupee depreciated beyond Rs.95/USD due to Strait of Hormuz geopolitical crude oil price pressures","RBI intervening in forex market via foreign exchange operations and liquidity tools","Middle-income trap risk: jobless growth, stagnant real wages, weak private investment"]', 'India maintained its position as world\'s fastest-growing major economy with 7.8% GDP growth in Q1 FY2026-27 (April-June 2026).

External headwinds intensified as the Rupee fell beyond Rs.95/USD driven by rising crude oil prices from Strait of Hormuz geopolitical tensions. Economists raised concerns about jobless growth and weak private investment despite strong GDP headline numbers. RBI actively managed forex volatility through market interventions.', 'High priority for UPSC GS-III (Economy), RBI Grade B, SBI PO, IBPS Banking Awareness. Monetary policy, GDP, and rupee are standard exam topics.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1611974789855-9c2a0a7236a3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'Economy', '["UPSC","Banking","RBI Grade B","SSC","State PSC"]', '["GDP Growth","RBI","Rupee Depreciation","Monetary Policy","Indian Economy"]', 'https://mospi.gov.in', '2026-09-14 18:30:00.000', 1, 1, NULL, '2026-09-22 17:23:10.951', '2026-09-22 17:23:10.951'),
  ('a87d9aa6-5fb8-4489-bac1-4eba922bda39', 'India Joins P4M (Partners for Multilateralism) at 81st UN General Assembly 2026', 'India co-sponsored the Partners for Multilateralism (P4M) initiative at UNGA-81 in September 2026 to advance UN80 reform and provide a middle-power alternative to superpower bloc polarization.', '["P4M (Partners for Multilateralism) launched at 81st UNGA, September 2026","India is initial co-sponsor alongside other middle-power democracies","Aims to advance UN80 reform (80th UN anniversary) for more representative global governance","Alternative to polarization between US-led West and China-Russia axis","Aligns with India\'s Strategic Autonomy foreign policy doctrine"]', 'India joined as an initial co-sponsor of the Partners for Multilateralism (P4M) initiative at the 81st UN General Assembly in New York, September 2026.

The P4M coalition of middle-power democracies seeks to advance the UN80 reform process and provide a pragmatic multilateral alternative beyond current superpower polarization.', 'Key for UPSC GS-II (International Organizations, India Foreign Policy). Multilateralism and India\'s global role are standard mains and prelims topics.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1541872703-74c5e44368f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'International', '["UPSC","State PSC","Law Exams","Diplomatic Services"]', '["UN General Assembly","Multilateralism","P4M","India Foreign Policy","UN Reform"]', 'https://mea.gov.in', '2026-09-19 18:30:00.000', 1, 1, NULL, '2026-09-22 17:23:10.954', '2026-09-22 17:23:10.954'),
  ('26dc33df-dbe3-4432-85dd-9b52f40f9284', '72nd National Film Awards Sept 22, 2026: Anant Nag (Dadasaheb Phalke), Article 370 Best Film', 'Ceremony at Ekta Nagar, Gujarat on Sept 22, 2026. Dadasaheb Phalke: Anant Nag. Best Actor (shared): Mammootty & Kartik Aaryan. Best Actress: Yami Gautam. Best Film: Article 370.', '["Ceremony: September 22, 2026, Ekta Nagar (Kevadia), Gujarat — presented by President Droupadi Murmu","Dadasaheb Phalke Award: Veteran actor Anant Nag (Kannada/Hindi cinema icon, 5 decades)","Best Actor (shared): Mammootty (Bramayugam) and Kartik Aaryan (Chandu Champion)","Best Actress: Yami Gautam — film Article 370","Best Feature Film: Article 370"]', 'The 72nd National Film Awards ceremony was held on September 22, 2026 at Ekta Nagar (Kevadia), Gujarat, with President Droupadi Murmu presenting the honors.

Veteran actor Anant Nag, celebrated for five decades in Kannada and Hindi cinema, received the Dadasaheb Phalke Award — India\'s highest cinematic recognition. \'Article 370\' dominated major categories.', 'Awards and appointments are heavily tested in SSC CGL, IBPS PO/Clerk, Railway NTPC General Awareness sections.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1478720568477-152d9b164e26?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'Awards & Persons', '["SSC","Banking","Railway","UPSC","State PSC"]', '["National Film Awards","Dadasaheb Phalke","Anant Nag","Bollywood","Awards 2026"]', 'https://pib.gov.in', '2026-09-21 18:30:00.000', 1, 1, NULL, '2026-09-22 17:23:10.957', '2026-09-22 17:23:10.957'),
  ('3e34331b-df73-469d-8547-b50c36721343', 'Asian Games 2026 Aichi-Nagoya: India Wins Cricket Gold, Suchika Tariyal Makes MMA History', 'Asian Games 2026 (Sept 19 - Oct 4, Aichi-Nagoya, Japan). India Women win cricket gold defeating Sri Lanka. Suchika Tariyal wins India\'s first-ever Asian Games MMA medal. Smriti Mandhana scores 11,000 international runs milestone.', '["Host: Aichi-Nagoya, Japan. Dates: September 19 - October 4, 2026","India Women\'s Cricket Team won GOLD medal (defeated Sri Lanka)","Suchika Tariyal — India\'s FIRST-EVER Asian Games medal in Mixed Martial Arts (MMA)","Savita Punia: Most-capped Indian women hockey player (320+ international caps)","Smriti Mandhana: First woman cricketer globally to complete 11,000 international runs"]', 'The 2026 Asian Games in Aichi-Nagoya, Japan (September 19 - October 4, 2026) marked landmark achievements for India.

The Indian women\'s cricket team won gold by defeating Sri Lanka. MMA athlete Suchika Tariyal created history winning India\'s first-ever Asian Games MMA medal. Women\'s hockey goalkeeper Savita Punia surpassed 320 international caps. Smriti Mandhana became the first woman cricketer globally to complete 11,000 international runs.', 'Sports GA is heavily tested in SSC, Railway, Banking exams. Asian Games hosts, firsts, and Indian medal winners are standard exam questions.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461896836934-ffe607ba8211?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'Sports', '["SSC","Railway","Banking","UPSC","State PSC"]', '["Asian Games 2026","India Sports","MMA","Women Cricket Gold","Aichi-Nagoya"]', 'https://olympic.ind.in', '2026-09-21 18:30:00.000', 1, 1, NULL, '2026-09-22 17:23:10.961', '2026-09-22 17:23:10.961'),
  ('7bdb0c3c-89cc-4a12-8b35-88969d35858e', 'Article 371K Proposed for Ladakh: Directly Elected Legislative Body with Special Safeguards', 'Union Government proposed inserting new Article 371K into the Constitution to give Ladakh a directly elected UT-level legislative body with financial and administrative powers.', '["Proposed: New Article 371K in Indian Constitution for Ladakh UT","Ladakh became UT without legislature after J&K reorganization in October 2019","Demands from Apex Body Leh (ABL) and Kargil Democratic Alliance (KDA)","Proposed body to have legislative, financial, and administrative powers","Part of India\'s asymmetric federalism debate — different constitutional arrangements for different regions"]', 'The Union Government proposed inserting Article 371K into the Constitution of India to give Ladakh special constitutional safeguards, including a directly elected legislative body.

This follows negotiations with representative bodies from Leh and Kargil. Since Ladakh became a UT without legislature in 2019, there have been sustained demands for democratic representation comparable to other UTs like Delhi and Puducherry.', 'Very important for UPSC GS-II (Indian Constitution, Federalism, Governance). Article 371 special provisions and UT administration are standard prelims and mains questions.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1566438480900-0609be27a4be?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'Politics', '["UPSC","State PSC","Law Exams","CLAT"]', '["Ladakh","Article 371","Constitution","Federalism","Governance"]', 'https://pib.gov.in', '2026-09-17 18:30:00.000', 1, 0, NULL, '2026-09-22 17:23:10.963', '2026-09-22 17:23:10.963'),
  ('1b525d01-e324-4d52-a555-fb6eb9387b1a', 'RBI Repo Rate at 5.25% in Sept 2026 Review; GDP Projected at 7.2% for FY2026-27', 'RBI MPC kept repo rate unchanged at 5.25% in September 2026 bi-monthly review. CPI inflation rising; GDP growth projected at 7.2% for FY2026-27. RBI monitoring crude oil impact on currency.', '["RBI Repo Rate: 5.25% (unchanged); SDF: 5.00%; MSF: 5.50%","CPI inflation rising for 3 consecutive months; food inflation elevated","GDP growth projection: 7.2% for FY2026-27","RBI monitoring crude oil price impact on rupee and inflation","New liquidity window announced for Green Energy bonds and infrastructure"]', 'The Reserve Bank of India\'s Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) kept the policy repo rate unchanged at 5.25% at its September 2026 bi-monthly review, maintaining a neutral stance.

The RBI Governor acknowledged CPI inflation rising for three consecutive months with elevated food prices. Despite this, the MPC held rates to assess the global commodity price trajectory and oil import impact on India\'s external account.', 'RBI monetary policy is mandatory knowledge for RBI Grade B, SBI PO, IBPS Banking Awareness, and UPSC Economy GS-III.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1567427017947-545c5f8d16ad?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'Economy', '["Banking","RBI Grade B","UPSC","SSC","State PSC"]', '["RBI","Repo Rate","Monetary Policy","CPI Inflation","GDP"]', 'https://rbi.org.in', '2026-09-09 18:30:00.000', 1, 1, NULL, '2026-09-22 17:23:10.966', '2026-09-22 17:23:10.966'),
  ('8546a14f-d71f-4536-8119-59e44f49fa8c', 'PM Vishwakarma Scheme Marks 3rd Anniversary — Rs.3 Lakh Credit to 18 Artisan Communities', 'PM Vishwakarma scheme completes 3 years (launched Sept 17, 2023). Provides up to Rs.3 lakh collateral-free credit at 5% interest, skill training, and GeM market access to 18 traditional artisan communities.', '["Launched: September 17, 2023; 3rd anniversary in September 2026","Covers 18 traditional artisan/craftsperson communities (Vishwakarma communities)","Credit: Up to Rs.3 lakh at 5% concessional interest (Rs.1L + Rs.2L tranches)","Training: 5-15 days basic + advanced training with daily stipend of Rs.500","Market access through Government e-Marketplace (GeM) and digital payment integration"]', 'PM Vishwakarma scheme, launched September 17, 2023, celebrated its 3rd anniversary in September 2026. Administered by Ministry of MSME, it covers 18 traditional artisan communities including carpenters, cobblers, blacksmiths, potters, weavers, and goldsmiths.

Key benefits: skill upgradation, collateral-free loans at 5% concessional interest, modern toolkits (up to Rs.15,000), and digital onboarding for GeM market access.', 'Government schemes with key financial figures are heavily tested in SSC CGL, IBPS PO, Railway NTPC, and all competitive exams.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1556761175-5973dc0f32e7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'Schemes & Policies', '["SSC","Banking","Railway","UPSC","State PSC"]', '["PM Vishwakarma","MSME","Artisans","Government Schemes","Skill India"]', 'https://pmvishwakarma.gov.in', '2026-09-16 18:30:00.000', 1, 0, NULL, '2026-09-22 17:23:10.968', '2026-09-22 17:23:10.968'),
  ('82ca438b-95f1-472e-859d-0de02cee49dc', '20th Rozgar Mela Distributes Appointment Letters; 12.75 Lakh Total Govt Jobs Under Initiative', 'The 20th Rozgar Mela held September 19, 2026 distributed government appointment letters to recruits, taking the total under the initiative to 12.75 lakh across central government departments.', '["20th Rozgar Mela: September 19, 2026","PM Modi distributed letters to over 51,000 recruits at this edition","Total appointment letters since initiative launch: 12.75 lakh (1.275 million)","Covers: Railways, Income Tax, India Post, Defence, Health, Education, CAPFs","Initiative launched to accelerate central government recruitment and reduce vacancies"]', 'The 20th Rozgar Mela on September 19, 2026 distributed government appointment letters to new recruits, bringing the cumulative total to approximately 12.75 lakh across central government departments.

The Rozgar Mela covers appointments in Railways, Income Tax Department, India Post, Ministry of Defence, Ministry of Health, and Central Armed Police Forces. The initiative was launched to fast-track central government recruitment.', 'Government employment schemes and central government recruitment are tested in UPSC GS-II, State PSC, SSC, and Railway current affairs sections.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1521791136064-7986c2920216?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'Schemes & Policies', '["UPSC","SSC","Banking","Railway","State PSC"]', '["Rozgar Mela","Government Employment","PM Initiative","Appointments"]', 'https://pib.gov.in', '2026-09-18 18:30:00.000', 1, 0, NULL, '2026-09-22 17:23:10.971', '2026-09-22 17:23:10.971'),
  ('7c23b2b7-72b6-4307-8b39-779d2594f6c9', 'SCO Trade Ministers Meet in Tajikistan: India Endorses 2026-2030 Action Plan', 'India participated in the 25th SCO Ministers meeting on foreign trade in Tajikistan (Sept 17, 2026), endorsing the SCO 2026-2030 Multilateral Trade and Economic Cooperation Action Plan.', '["25th SCO Ministers meeting on trade held in Dushanbe, Tajikistan, September 17, 2026","India endorsed SCO\'s 2026-2030 Multilateral Trade & Economic Cooperation Action Plan","Focus areas: Digital trade, green economy, supply chain resilience, energy cooperation","SCO covers 40%+ of world population and 30%+ of global GDP","India is full SCO member since 2017 (alongside China, Russia, Pakistan, Central Asian states)"]', 'India participated in the 25th Meeting of SCO Ministers responsible for foreign economic and trade activities held in Dushanbe, Tajikistan on September 17, 2026.

The meeting endorsed the SCO 2026-2030 Multilateral Trade and Economic Cooperation Action Plan, covering digital trade, green economy transition, supply chain diversification, and energy cooperation.', 'SCO is a highly tested topic in UPSC GS-II (International Relations, Regional Organizations). India in multilateral economic forums is regularly examined.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529107386315-e1a2ed48a620?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'International', '["UPSC","State PSC","Banking","SSC"]', '["SCO","Shanghai Cooperation Organisation","Trade Policy","Multilateralism","Tajikistan"]', 'https://mea.gov.in', '2026-09-16 18:30:00.000', 1, 0, NULL, '2026-09-22 17:23:10.974', '2026-09-22 17:23:10.974'),
  ('c7977964-518c-4f1b-bc6d-0a46de947b66', 'Swachh Sagar Surakshit Sagar 5.0: 15 Lakh Pledge Ocean Conservation Across 231 Sites', 'India\'s 5th edition of Swachh Sagar Surakshit Sagar (Sept 12-19, 2026) saw 15 lakh participants at 231 coastal sites in 13 States/UTs pledge for ocean conservation.', '["5th edition: September 12-19, 2026 across 231 coastal locations in 13 States/UTs","15 lakh (1.5 million) participants took the Ocean Conservation Pledge","Campaign by Ministry of Earth Sciences (MoES) and NCPOR","Focus: Marine debris removal, blue economy awareness, coastal ecosystem protection","Aligns with India\'s National Action Plan for Marine Litter and UN SDG-14 (Life Below Water)"]', 'The 5th edition of Swachh Sagar Surakshit Sagar ran from September 12-19, 2026, organized by the Ministry of Earth Sciences and NCPOR.

Over 15 lakh citizens participated across 231 coastal sites in 13 States/UTs, collecting marine litter and pledging ocean conservation. The campaign aligns with India\'s National Action Plan for Marine Litter and UN SDG-14.', 'Environment & Ecology, government schemes, and coastal conservation are standard topics for UPSC GS-3 Prelims, SSC, and Banking GA.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1502126324834-38f8e02d7160?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'Environment', '["UPSC","SSC","Banking","Railway","NDA"]', '["Swachh Sagar","Ocean Conservation","Environment","Coastal India","Government Schemes"]', 'https://incois.gov.in', '2026-09-18 18:30:00.000', 1, 0, NULL, '2026-09-22 17:23:10.981', '2026-09-22 17:23:10.981');

